<title>UK: EBRD buys 23 percent stake in Latvian bank.</title>
<headline>EBRD buys 23 percent stake in Latvian bank.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development has paid $6.0 million for a 23 percent stake in Latvia's third largest bank, Rigas Komercbanka.</p>
<p>&quot;The EBRD achieves two of its priorities in Latvia with this investment in Rigas Komercbanka. First strengthening the capital base of one of Latvia's leading private sector banks and secondly, facilitating the flow of capital to the corporate sector,&quot; said David Hexter deputy vice president said.</p>
<p>The EBRD will acquire 2,669,702 newly issued common shares in the bank.</p>
<p>The bank has 728 employees and 11 branches and the EBRD will get two seats on the supervisory board.</p>
<p>-- David Chance London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
